":"billuo","id":43804776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzODA0Nzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43804776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo","html_url":"https://github.com/billuo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/billuo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-07T11:28:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T11:28:09Z","body":"Can't replicate with the MRP, but can somewhat replicate with a larger atlas (784x352 image of 16x16 tiles, 1078 tiles in total).\n> Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.90 GiB memory\n\nThough even with the larger atlas, it does not lag to the point of being unusable on my machine, the frame drop is certainly noticeable. Task manager shows that whenever I move the cursor inside the tile set editor in paint mode, CPU usage of the editor spikes. With the original MRP it's better: I can't notice any lag, but CPU usage still noticeably goes up.\n\nA quick debug led me to this:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/220b0b2f74d8e089481b140c42a42992a76dd6fc/editor/scene/2d/tiles/tile_set_atlas_source_editor.cpp#L1083-L1101\nIt basically redraws *everything* upon a `gui_input` event in painting mode. It can certainly do better with a proper dirty flag, b